id: pm-web-4p94
title: Default catalog freshness tests interpret a partial sibling worktree farm as the complete fleet
description: "Fixed in PR #226: catalog freshness reads a sibling farm only when PM_FLEET_ROOT is explicitly configured. Default committed roster, snapshot, native-command and synthetic discovery checks remain enabled; an explicit incomplete farm still fails. The ambient partial-farm regression fails with the default-selection fix reverted and passes when restored. Child node:test contexts are cleared so subprocess assertions execute. Focused tests pass 38/38; actual CI with PM_FLEET_ROOT unset passes both npm and Bun full gates on Node 22 and 26, each 677/677. No catalog snapshots, pins or thresholds changed."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[2]: catalog,testing
created_at: "2026-10-15T23:07:53.640Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T19:52:02.036Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T11:26:38.059Z",codex-agent,"Related fleet-root workaround caveat reproduced during pm-web-pep7: a relative PM_FLEET_ROOT reaches scripts/read-fleet-commands.ts without normalization, so the dependency symlink created inside a disposable package copy points relative to that copy instead of the source checkout. The optional command-snapshot test then reports a missing @typesafe-ai/sdk dependency for Jev despite the canonical checkout dependency being present. Resolving the same fleet root at invocation time made the complete command-snapshot check pass. Follow-up: normalize the configured fleet root before constructing disposable dependency symlinks, alongside the existing partial-sibling root-selection work. No implementation or threshold changes for this follow-up."
  "2026-10-17T11:01:31.050Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 release attempts provide a controlled topology comparison: the package worktree fails catalog membership and live-fleet snapshot equality, while an isolated standalone copy passes those same checks. All 258 TypeScript/CSS source files were verified byte-identical between the two copies, and both use fresh HOME with global/system Git config disabled. The standalone profile matches CI and uses independent test storage. No catalog source, fixture roster, snapshot or test condition changed."
  "2026-10-19T18:20:53.351Z",codex-agent,"Checking whether catalog freshness reads ambient sibling packages. Will make external fleet validation explicit, retain committed snapshot invariants and synthetic farm coverage, and run both release gates with PM_FLEET_ROOT unset."
  "2026-10-19T18:20:55.939Z",codex-agent,"Will make external fleet reads explicit, preserve committed snapshot invariants and synthetic farm coverage, and run npm/Bun release gates with PM_FLEET_ROOT unset."
  "2026-10-19T18:30:39.913Z",codex-agent,"Hermetic regression passes with an ambient synthetic unpublished sibling and PM_FLEET_ROOT unset, but rejects the same farm when explicitly selected. Reverting catalog.test.ts to origin/main fails the new default-isolation assertion. Child node:test contexts are cleared so the synthetic standalone and explicit-farm assertions actually execute. Committed roster/snapshot invariants remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T18:36:09.447Z",codex-agent,"Linked catalog/fleet command completed with PM_FLEET_ROOT unset: 38/38 pass, zero failures/cancelled/skipped/todo. Explicit synthetic-farm checks execute in a fresh node:test context; no ambient fleet snapshots or dependency pins were changed."
  "2026-10-19T18:54:54.053Z",codex-agent,"The first full isolated-home npm run with PM_FLEET_ROOT unset passed every catalog/fleet test; all five original freshness failures are resolved. Its one unrelated-to-catalog failure is the new HTTP event payload field, being removed while preserving internal receipts."
  "2026-10-19T19:51:45.123Z",codex-agent,"Actual CI proof with PM_FLEET_ROOT unset is green at ad380c7 on both Node 22 and 26: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 677/677 tests, 2/2 capacity scenarios and 4/4 packed consumers with zero production vulnerabilities. Both CI jobs pass strict tracker health, fresh-build parity, changelog and release-attestation checks. Local host timing failures are separately retained in pm-web-qdhx."
